-- Feser's Aristotelian Proof in Term Functor Logic
-- Five Proofs of the Existence of God, ch. 1
--
-- TFL extends the SYL version in three ways:
--
--   (1) Relational terms: "X is actualized BY Y" is a genuine
--       two-place predicate with positional subscripts, not
--       the monadic substitute ActualizedByAnother.
--
--   (2) Sorites: multi-premise chains in a single proof block
--       condense what required three separate SYL proofs.
--
--   (3) Complement terms: non-Potential, non-Differentiable
--       encode privation directly in the term algebra.

rel Actualize "Actualizer-of" "Actualized-by"

-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- PART I: THE CAUSAL CHAIN (relational)
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
--
-- This proof cannot be expressed in SYL at all. It states the
-- causal structure of the argument using two-place relational
-- terms with positional subscripts.
--
-- P1: Whatever changes is being actualized by some actualizer.
--     (From the act/potency analysis: change = transition from
--     potential to actual; a potency cannot actualize itself.)
--
-- P2: Every actualizer belongs to an essentially ordered causal
--     series (one in which each intermediate member has only
--     derivative causal power).
--
-- P3: An essentially ordered series cannot regress to infinity;
--     it requires a first member whose causal power is underived.
--
-- P4: Some things really do change. (To deny this is self-
--     refuting: the denial is itself a change of mind.)
--
-- Cancellation:
--   +Actualizer<1>  (P1) cancels  -Actualizer<1>  (P2)
--   +InEOSeries<1>  (P2) cancels  -InEOSeries<1>  (P3)
--   -Changing<2>    (P1) cancels  +Changing<2>    (P4)
--
-- What remains uncancelled:
--   +Being<2>  +Actualize<1,2>  +FirstActualizer<1>
--
-- Read: some being is actualized by some first actualizer.

proof ExistenceOfFirstActualizer
  -Changing<2> +Actualize<1,2> +Actualizer<1>
  -Actualizer<1> +InEOSeries<1>
  -InEOSeries<1> +FirstActualizer<1>
  +Being<2> +Changing<2>
  ∴ +Being<2> +Actualize<1,2> +FirstActualizer<1>

-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- PART II: FROM CHANGE TO PURE ACTUALITY (monadic sorites)
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
--
-- TFL sorites condense the three separate SYL proofs
-- (ChangeIsActualization, SeriesRequiresFirst,
-- ChangingDependsOnFirst) into a single four-premise chain.

proof ChangingDependsOnFirst
  every HavingPotentialActualized is ActualizedByAnother
  every Changing is HavingPotentialActualized
  every InEssentiallyOrderedSeries is DependentOnFirst
  every ActualizedByAnother is InEssentiallyOrderedSeries
  ∴ every Changing is DependentOnFirst

-- Some things really do change.

proof SomeThingsChange
  @ChangingDependsOnFirst
  some Being is Changing
  ∴ some Being is DependentOnFirst

-- The first actualizer has no unactualized potentials (else it
-- would need a prior actualizer and not be first). So it is
-- purely actual.

proof FirstIsPurelyActual
  every FirstActualizer is PurelyActual
  some Being is FirstActualizer
  ∴ some Being is PurelyActual

-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- PART III: DIVINE ATTRIBUTES
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
--
-- From pure actuality the classical divine attributes follow.
-- Each derivation uses complement terms (non-P) where Feser's
-- argument turns on the absence of a feature.

-- No potentiality entails no capacity for change.

proof PurelyActualIsImmutable
  every non-Potential is Immutable
  every PurelyActual is non-Potential
  ∴ every PurelyActual is Immutable

-- What cannot change is outside of time.

proof PurelyActualIsEternal
  every Immutable is Eternal
  @PurelyActualIsImmutable
  ∴ every PurelyActual is Eternal

-- Matter involves potentiality; a purely actual being has none.

proof PurelyActualIsImmaterial
  every Material is Potential
  no PurelyActual is Potential
  ∴ no PurelyActual is Material

-- Lacking no actuality, a purely actual being is perfect.

proof PurelyActualIsPerfect
  every FullyActual is Perfect
  every PurelyActual is FullyActual
  ∴ every PurelyActual is Perfect

-- If two purely actual beings existed, one would need to lack
-- what the other has — i.e. have unactualized potential —
-- contradicting pure actuality.

proof PurelyActualIsUnique
  every non-Differentiable is Unique
  every PurelyActual is non-Differentiable
  ∴ every PurelyActual is Unique

-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- PART IV: EXISTENTIAL CONCLUSIONS
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
--
-- Apply the existential result (some being is purely actual)
-- to each attribute.

proof SomeBeingIsImmutable
  @PurelyActualIsImmutable
  @FirstIsPurelyActual
  ∴ some Being is Immutable

proof SomeBeingIsEternal
  @PurelyActualIsEternal
  @FirstIsPurelyActual
  ∴ some Being is Eternal

proof SomeBeingIsImmaterial
  @PurelyActualIsImmaterial
  @FirstIsPurelyActual
  ∴ some Being is not Material

proof SomeBeingIsPerfect
  @PurelyActualIsPerfect
  @FirstIsPurelyActual
  ∴ some Being is Perfect

proof SomeBeingIsUnique
  @PurelyActualIsUnique
  @FirstIsPurelyActual
  ∴ some Being is Unique
